  m_Name: Part_back_shell
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OrionAR.PartInfo
  partId: back_shell
  displayName: Back Shell and Thermal Protection
  shortName: Back Shell
  zone: 0
  order: 20
  keySpec: "Blunt 57.5\xB0 cone  \xB7  ~1,300 tiles"
  summary: The cone covering everything above the heat shield. It does not face the
    fiercest heating, but it must survive vacuum, micrometeoroid strikes and a swing
    of hundreds of degrees between sunlight and shadow.
  whyItMatters: The blunt shape is deliberately poor aerodynamics. A pointed nose
    would hug its own shock wave; a blunt body pushes a detached bow shock well ahead
    of the vehicle, so the atmosphere absorbs most of the entry energy instead of
    the spacecraft.
  narration: {fileID: 0}
